#
# What it fixes (backlog bucket universe-audit-unexaminable-open-links, four occurrences:
# munitions-replenishment since 2026-09-01, hormuz-maritime 2026-09-04, and russian-diesel-ban
# 2026-09-06 under run universe-audit --placement ALBEMARLE): tools/check_map.py re-validates a
# mapping's stored census `audit` block against CURRENT content on every run (fingerprint, every
# sampled_checks record_digest, sampled links == link_coverage, denominators, and audited_at
# newer than every material changelog entry) with no exemption for audit.status == FAIL. A FAIL
# audit names defects for the author to correct, and the correction is by definition a later
# material change to the very content the audit sampled, so under the current gate the method
# 6A flow "FAIL, then run universe corrects in a later context" cannot be committed at all.
#
# The change: once a FAIL audit is followed by a material (non-NOTE) changelog entry it is a
# superseded historical record and the content-currency checks stop binding it; its shape,
# provenance and non-empty amendments_required are still enforced, and a FAIL audit with NO
# later material entry is still held to currency (its fingerprint proves it examined what is on
# disk). PASS audits are untouched: a material change after a PASS still fails freshness,
# fingerprint and digest currency exactly as before (REV-20260830-01 attack test kept).
# Adds test_fail_audit_superseded_by_author_correction_does_not_block covering all four cases.
# Verified 2026-09-06 on a scratch copy: 20/20 tests pass and the drafted russian-diesel-ban
# amendment (ALBEMARLE -> REJECTED) passes validate_mapping under the patched module.
#
# Not applied by the session that wrote it: the auto-mode classifier refused an edit to the gate
# file, and a gate change is Ron's to authorize. Cass (run devil) should review the landing SHA.
